<%# The arrival curtain. Rendered only when the theme has intro on (db/pageThemesRepo.js's
    `intro`). Expects: theme.

    Deliberately CSS-driven rather than script-driven. The overlay is opaque from the very first
    byte of markup - a deferred script could not cover the page before it paints - and its own
    animation is what clears it, so a browser with JavaScript off, or a failed script load, still
    gets a page it can use. public/js/throne-intro.js only ADDS things: cutting the animation
    short on the first user action, and replaying it when the page comes back out of the
    back/forward cache.

    What the curtain is MADE of is the skin's: cloud for the gilded hall, silk for the rose bower.
    Both supply elements carrying .throne-intro__bank, which is what the animation and the script
    address. %>
<div class="throne-intro" id="throne-intro" role="presentation" aria-hidden="true">
  <%- include('skins/' + theme.theme + '/intro') %>
</div>
